day unlike Retinol which reacts to sun exposure.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:15px;\">- A patch test helps rule out possible allergic reactions.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:15px;\">- It can suit people with delicate or dry skin, but mild peeling may occur.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggSjivuWvHc_label","label":"ggSjivuWvHc_label","default":"Buy It Now"},{"type":"html","id":"ggQQstHvxMk_text","label":"ggQQstHvxMk_text","default":"What is Bakuchiol Serum?"},{"type":"html","id":"gggAvq1w7r8_text","label":"gggAvq1w7r8_text","default":"<p>Many see bakuchiol serum as a gentler option for improving skin. It comes from the Babchi plant, known in traditional Chinese and Indian&nbsp;<br>medicine for its soothing qualities. People often look into the side effects of bakuchiol serum as a natural alternative to retinol.</p><p><br><strong>Definition and Origin</strong></p><p>Bakuchiol comes from the purple-blossomed Babchi plant. It has been valued for centuries. Skincare enthusiasts love it for its gentle yet effective approach.</p><p>Brands see its promise in reducing fine lines and making skin look younger. They know it's gentler than stronger actives.<br><br><strong>Common Uses in Skincare</strong></p><p>Serums, creams, and moisturizers often include bakuchiol. They aim to tackle mature skin concerns and uneven tone. Its popularity grows as it's seen<br>&nbsp;as less irritating yet effective. &nbsp;Some love how it brightens dull areas and smooths out texture issues. It's a supportive ingredient in many skincare products.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggMdkkW8U5K_label","label":"ggMdkkW8U5K_label","default":"Buy It Now"},{"type":"html","id":"gguH45fppc2_text","label":"gguH45fppc2_text","default":"How Does Bakuchiol Work?&nbsp;"},{"type":"html","id":"ggqMpk7UepX_text","label":"ggqMpk7UepX_text","default":"<p>This plant-based active encourages cell turnover and spurs collagen production. It's a gentler option for those seeking a new approach. But, it's wise to do a patch test first, as any new product&nbsp;<br>can have risks. Experts say bakuchiol serum side effects are usually mild. But, you might experience dryness or tightness sometimes. Research shows it works like retinol, improving texture and fine lines.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Mechanism of Action</strong></p><p>This soothing molecule works with skin receptors to promote healthy regeneration. It starts gently, with less peeling, which can be less uncomfortable. Regular use often leads to a smoother complexion.<br>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Comparison to Retinol</strong></p><p>Both ingredients target aging signs, but bakuchiol is better for sensitive skin. It has a similar effect on collagen but is gentler on delicate areas.&nbsp;</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggV0mgB8Gbt_label","label":"ggV0mgB8Gbt_label","default":"Buy It Now"}],
